<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document>
<name>Cleveland Shortlist — 19 stops over 3 days</name>
<description>The original hand-picked shortlist. Import into Google My Maps: My Maps > Create a new map > Import.</description>
<Folder><name>Day 1 — Downtown Core (walkable)</name>
<Placemark><name>Soldiers' &amp; Sailors' Monument</name><description>3 Public Square

Suggested: 10:00 AM
Free inside. The tunnel labyrinth underneath opens one day a year — ask at the desk.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6929283,41.4995228,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Chess Collection, Cleveland Public Library</name><description>325 Superior Ave NE, 3rd floor

Suggested: 10:45 AM
World's largest chess collection. Photo ID; one item at a time. Closed Sunday.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6916133,41.501113,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Arcade</name><description>401 Euclid Ave

Suggested: 11:45 AM
1890 glass-roofed arcade modelled on Milan's Galleria. Lunch inside.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6902444,41.4999444,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Terminal Tower Observation Deck</name><description>50 Public Square

Suggested: 1:00 PM
Weekends only, ~$5–6, tickets online in advance. No walk-ups.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6939263,41.4983959,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Free Stamp</name><description>Willard Park, 601 Lakeside Ave E

Suggested: 2:30 PM
Oldenburg &amp; van Bruggen's giant rubber stamp. Two minutes, always open.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6924552,41.5054252,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>USS Cod Submarine Memorial</name><description>1201 N Marginal Rd

Suggested: 3:15 PM
Last intact WWII fleet sub. Entry down a vertical ladder — not accessible.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6915676,41.5100715,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 2 — University Circle &amp; East Side</name>
<Placemark><name>Percy Skuy Collection, Dittrick Medical History Center</name><description>11000 Euclid Ave

Suggested: 11:00 AM
Fri 10:30–4 and Sat 12–4 ONLY. Free. 1,000+ contraceptive artifacts.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.608414,41.5059193,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cleveland Museum of Art</name><description>11150 East Blvd

Suggested: 1:00 PM
Free. Enter from Wade Park for the view across the lagoon. Closed Monday.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6119723,41.5079261,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cleveland Museum of Natural History</name><description>1 Wade Oval Dr

Suggested: 2:30 PM
Lucy, Balto, and an Apollo 12 moon rock. Closed Monday.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6130674,41.5114773,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Haserot Angel, Lake View Cemetery</name><description>12316 Euclid Ave · Section 9, Lot 14

Suggested: 4:00 PM
Grab a map at the gate. Nearest landmark is the Hanna Mausoleum.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.590375,41.513022,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Rockefeller Park Greenhouse</name><description>750 E 88th St

Suggested: Earlier
Closes at 4pm — swap earlier in the day. Free.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6287004,41.5370491,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Quintana's Speakeasy</name><description>2200 S Taylor Rd, Cleveland Heights

Suggested: 7:00 PM
Back door of the barbershop, buzzer, 'a man about a horse', then pull the right book.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.5563368,41.4998009,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 3 — West Side, Tremont &amp; South</name>
<Placemark><name>West Side Market</name><description>1979 W 25th St

Suggested: 9:00 AM
Bring cash. Closed Tuesday and Thursday. First hour parking free.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.7028394,41.4847078,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Buckland Museum of Witchcraft &amp; Magick</name><description>2155 Broadview Rd

Suggested: 12:30 PM
Gardner's artifacts, Sybil Leek's crystal ball, a demon in a box. Allow an hour.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6998196,41.43805,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>A Christmas Story House</name><description>3159 W 11th St

Suggested: 2:00 PM
Tours every 30 min from 10:15. Budget two hours.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.6874036,41.4687304,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>b.a. Sweetie Candy Company</name><description>6770 Brookpark Rd

Suggested: 3:30 PM
A warehouse of candy, plus a soda fountain.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.7316654,41.4201515,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Superelectric Pinball Parlor</name><description>6500 Detroit Ave

Suggested: 5:00 PM
Flat fee, unlimited play. Closed Tuesday.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.7304346,41.4842367,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Sanctuary Museum</name><description>12905 Madison Ave, Lakewood

Suggested: 6:00 PM
Wed mornings and Sat afternoons ONLY. Rescued church statuary.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.778332,41.4767072,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Solstice Steps, Lakewood Park</name><description>14532 Lake Ave, Lakewood

Suggested: 7:30 PM
Best sunset in the region. Arrive 30 min early for a lower terrace.</description><Point><coordinates>-81.797965,41.4972086,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
</Document></kml>